  "_botSpawns": "Every bot starts on the ground. Structures are somewhere bots MOVE to, never somewhere they begin: a squad that opens the round already on a roof reads as spawning in the sky and gives the player nothing to walk into. Positions were found by tools/ground-spawns and are re-checked by tools/map-validate.",
  "_flow": "The player's spawn had clear sight to an enemy spawn 89.3m away -- the single worst sightline in the game and, at that range, an enemy you cannot resolve shooting at you before you have moved. Two thickets screen it (concealment, so paint still passes and the lane stays honest) and two hard pieces break the middle. Measured by tools/flow-report.",
  "_verticality": "Two timber stands, not fire towers. Their decks were at 12.2m and 12.7m -- on a woods map that reads as climbing a building, and bots used to spawn up there. Both are stands on ground that is already high (hill_n tops at 4m, ridge_e at 5m), so the stand only ever needed to be a stand: decks now sit at 8.2m and 7.7m. hill_ne came down from 7m to 5.5m with them."
